{"id":"resp_82e38a730388e58a","created_at":1795618253,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_97b0c9f57f53714e","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to generate a SHACL shape graph representing the requirement.\n\nRequirement I2.1.2.2: ship displacement DUI is displacement in kt of the ship corresponding to UIWL. Where multiple waterlines are used for determining UIWL, displacement is to be determined from waterline corresponding to greatest displacement.\n\nThus we need constraints: ship must have property upperIceWaterlineDisplacement (quantity) representing displacement, unit kt. Also perhaps waterlineCaseDisplacement for each case, and property hasUpperIceWaterlineCase linking ship to upperIceWaterlineCase. The requirement says displacement corresponds to UIWL, choose greatest displacement among multiple waterlines. So we need to assert that for a ship, the upperIceWaterlineDisplacement must equal the maximum waterlineCaseDisplacement among its hasUpperIceWaterlineCase cases.\n\nIn SHACL, we can express using sh:property with sh:path to upperIceWaterlineDisplacement, sh:datatype decimal (via quantity). Need to represent quantity using qudt numericValue and unit. Use property shape for upperIceWaterlineDisplacement: expects a resource of type qudt:QuantityValue with numericValue decimal and unit KiloTON_Metric.\n\nAlso need a shape that computes max? SHACL doesn't have max over multiple values directly; but we can use sh:qualifiedValueShape with sh:count etc? Not direct. Could express constraint that each waterlineCaseDisplacement value must be <= upperIceWaterlineDisplacement, and at least one equals. Use sh:property with sh:path ??? Actually we can create shape for ship that has a property hasUpperIceWaterlineCase linking to cases; for each case, the waterlineCaseDisplacement's numeric value must be <= upperIceWaterlineDisplacement; and there must exist a case where it's equal.\n\nWe need to use quantityEncoding mapping: numeric predicate = http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/numericValue; unit predicate = http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unit.\n\nThus for a QuantityValue node, we need to check numericValue.\n\nDefine shapes:\n\nex:ShipShape a sh:NodeShape;\n    sh:targetClass <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship>;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineDisplacement>;\n        sh:nodeKind sh:IRI; # expects a QuantityValue instance\n        sh:class <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue>;\n        # maybe also check unit\n        sh:property [\n            sh:path <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unit>;\n            sh:hasValue <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloTON_Metric>;\n        ];\n        sh:property [\n            sh:path <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/numericValue>;\n            sh:datatype xsd:decimal;\n            # maybe nothing else\n        ];\n    ];\n\nNext shape for waterlineCaseDisplacement property.\n\nex:UpperIceWaterlineCaseShape a sh:NodeShape;\n    sh:targetClass <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineCase>;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#waterlineCaseDisplacement>;\n        sh:nodeKind sh:IRI;\n        sh:class <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue>;\n        sh:property [\n            sh:path <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unit>;\n            sh:hasValue <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloTON_Metric>;\n        ];\n    ];\n\nNow the constraint linking them: In ShipShape, we need to assert that there is at least one case where numericValue equals the ship's displacement numericValue, and all cases' numericValue <= ship's.\n\nWe can use sh:property for hasUpperIceWaterlineCase with qualified value shape.\n\nsh:property [\n    sh:path <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasUpperIceWaterlineCase>;\n    sh:qualifiedValueShape [\n        a sh:NodeShape;\n        sh:property [\n            sh:path <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#waterlineCaseDisplacement>;\n            sh:nodeKind sh:IRI;\n            sh:class <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue>;\n            # compare using sh:equals? SHACL can use sh:equals with node but not across nodes. Use sh:property with sh:lessThanOrEquals? There is SHACL Advanced Features: sh:lessThanOrEquals built-in? SPARQL-based constraints may be needed.\n\nAllowed to use sh:rule or sh:sparql.\n\nWe can define a sh:sparql constraint on ship:\n\nsh:sparql [\n    a sh:SPARQLConstraint;\n    sh:message \"Upper ice waterline displacement must be the maximum of waterline case displacements.\";\n    sh:select \"\"\"\n        SELECT $this (MAX(?caseVal) AS ?maxCase) ?shipVal WHERE {\n            $this <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineDisplacement> ?shipQty .\n            ?shipQty <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/numericValue> ?shipVal .\n            $this <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasUpperIceWaterlineCase> ?case .\n            ?case <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#waterlineCaseDisplacement> ?caseQty .\n            ?caseQty <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/numericValue> ?caseVal .\n        }\n        GROUP BY $this ?shipVal\n        HAVING ( ?shipVal != ?maxCase )\n    \"\"\" ;\n].\n\nBut SHACL SPARQLConstraint expects a SELECT that returns violating nodes; the HAVING condition returns rows where shipVal != maxCase, meaning violation.\n\nAlso ensure unit equality maybe.\n\nThus final SHACL graph includes prefixes, shapes, property constraints, and SPARQL.\n\nWe must include <BEGIN_SHACL> and <END_SHACL> markers.\n\nAlso need to note unresolved ownership: upperIceWaterline is unresolved, we won't target.\n\nWe must use exact IRIs.\n\nDefine prefixes: sh, xsd, rdf, rdfs, qudt, vocab.\n\nNow produce Turtle.\n\nMake sure to include sh:targetClass only if target_owner is given; contract target_owner null, but admission focus_set is owner_class ship, so we can target that class.\n\nThus final Answer: Provide SHACL.\n\n","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_ac2faebf3e5a65ca","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"<BEGIN_SHACL>\n@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .\n@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .\n@prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/> .\n@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .\n@prefix vocab: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n\n############################\n# Shape for Ship instances #\n############################\n\nvocab:ShipShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass vocab:ship ;\n    # ---- upperIceWaterlineDisplacement (Quantity) ----\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path vocab:upperIceWaterlineDisplacement ;\n        sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ;                     # expects a QuantityValue node\n        sh:class qudt:QuantityValue ;\n        # unit must be kt\n        sh:property [\n            sh:path qudt:unit ;\n            sh:hasValue unit:KiloTON_Metric ;\n        ] ;\n        # numeric value must be decimal\n        sh:property [\n            sh:path qudt:numericValue ;\n            sh:datatype xsd:decimal ;\n        ] ;\n    ] ;\n    # ---- hasUpperIceWaterlineCase relationships ----\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path vocab:hasUpperIceWaterlineCase ;\n        sh:class vocab:upperIceWaterlineCase ;\n    ] ;\n    # ---- SPARQL constraint: ship displacement must be the maximum of its waterline cases ----\n    sh:sparql [\n        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;\n        sh:message \"The upper‑ice‑waterline displacement (DUI) must equal the greatest displacement among the associated waterline cases.\" ;\n        sh:select \"\"\"\n            PREFIX sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#>\n            PREFIX vocab: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#>\n            PREFIX qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/>\n\n            SELECT $this WHERE {\n                $this vocab:upperIceWaterlineDisplacement ?shipQty .\n                ?shipQty qudt:numericValue ?shipVal .\n                $this vocab:hasUpperIceWaterlineCase ?case .\n                ?case vocab:waterlineCaseDisplacement ?caseQty .\n                ?caseQty qudt:numericValue ?caseVal .\n            }\n            GROUP BY $this ?shipVal\n            HAVING ( ?shipVal != MAX(?caseVal) )\n        \"\"\" ;\n    ] .\n\n######################################################\n# Shape for UpperIceWaterlineCase (design condition) #\n######################################################\n\nvocab:UpperIceWaterlineCaseShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass vocab:upperIceWaterlineCase ;\n    # ---- waterlineCaseDisplacement (Quantity) ----\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path vocab:waterlineCaseDisplacement ;\n        sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ;\n        sh:class qudt:QuantityValue ;\n        sh:property [\n            sh:path qudt:unit ;\n            sh:hasValue unit:KiloTON_Metric ;\n        ] ;\n        sh:property [\n            sh:path qudt:numericValue ;\n            sh:datatype xsd:decimal ;\n        ] ;\n    ] .\n\n#############################\n# Unresolved ownership note #\n#############################\n# The property vocab:upperIceWaterline is mentioned in the source but its ownership\n# cannot be resolved from the supplied ontology. No shape is generated for it,\n# preserving the ambiguity as required.\n\n<END_SHACL>","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":null,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":14109,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":592,"cache_write_tokens":13504,"input_tokens_per_turn":[14109],"cached_tokens_per_turn":[592]},"output_tokens":2149,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1350,"tool_output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_per_turn":[2149],"tool_output_tokens_per_turn":[0]},"total_tokens":16258},"user":null,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"input_messages":null,"output_messages":null}